OL,3,CUK economy races ahead of G7 pack in
OL,4,Cfirst half of 2026 despite Gulf war
OL,6,F"This is an active, hands-on
OL,7,Fgovernment, putting British interests
OL,8,Ffirst - giving breathing space to
OL,9,Fthose feeling the strain, making our
OL,10,Fcountry more resilient and bringing
OL,11,Fhope back," said Chancellor John Healy
OL,12,Fin a statement on Thursday.
OL,14,FIf a peace deal can be agreed between
OL,15,Fthe US and Iran, if the Strait of
OL,16,FHormuz can be sustainably reopened,
OL,17,Fand if the price of energy drops and
OL,18,Finflation fades - maybe the Bank of
OL,19,FEngland will begin to cut interest
OL,20,Frates. Why, things could get even
OL,21,Fbetter.
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@KO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31807
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1786709906
OL,3,CUK economy races ahead of G7 pack in
OL,4,Cfirst half of 2026 despite Gulf war
OL,6,FOf course, none of the above may
OL,7,Fhappen. Things could get worse.
OL,9,FWage growth in the UK is already
OL,10,Fslowing. The price of petrol has risen
OL,11,F11p a litre in the last month to a new
OL,12,Fpeak since the war began.
OL,14,FMost economists expect inflation to
OL,15,Fedge up further in the months ahead,
OL,16,Falong with unemployment, which is one
OL,17,Freason why Burnham is making so much
OL,18,Fof leading a "cost-of-living
OL,19,Fgovernment".
OL,26,@zD@NOU{D@KO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31808
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1786709906
OL,3,CUK economy races ahead of G7 pack in
OL,4,Cfirst half of 2026 despite Gulf war
OL,6,FHe is already hard-selling relatively
OL,7,Fcheap giveaways - bus fare freezes and
OL,8,FVAT cuts to energy bills, a modest tax
OL,9,Fcut for pubs - as very big deals and
OL,10,Fwe can expect more support to come in
OL,11,Fthe Budget in October.
OL,13,FIn recent years, endless pre-Budget
OL,14,Fspeculation about tax rises and who
OL,15,Fwill be targeted has been deeply
OL,16,Funhelpful - making businesses cautious
OL,17,Fabout investing and taking people on.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31809
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1786709906
OL,3,CUK economy races ahead of G7 pack in
OL,4,Cfirst half of 2026 despite Gulf war
OL,6,FWe still don't have a clear idea of
OL,7,Fwhat Andy Burnham's tax and spending
OL,8,Fplans are. The campfire gossip is that
OL,9,Fthere are some hefty tax rises coming.
OL,11,FIt's certainly hard to reconcile his
OL,12,Fstated ambitions - more public control
OL,13,Fof public services, a council
OL,14,Fhousebuilding revival, reform of
OL,15,Fsocial care - with the state of the
OL,16,Fgovernment's finances.
OL,18,FIt will be interesting to see how
OL,19,FNumber 10 decides to manage the weeks
OL,20,Fahead.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31810
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1786709906
OL,3,CUK economy races ahead of G7 pack in
OL,4,Cfirst half of 2026 despite Gulf war
OL,6,FIt's worth remembering that we are now
OL,7,Ftwo years into a Labour government
OL,8,Fthat swept to victory on a pledge to
OL,9,Frevive economic growth and deliver
OL,10,Fprosperity that households would feel
OL,11,Fin time for the next election.
OL,13,F"The highest sustained economic growth
OL,14,Fin the G7" is what Labour promised.
OL,15,FMiddle-of-the-pack is what we have got
OL,16,Fso far, however you measure it.
OL,26,@uD@AOUvD@JO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31811
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1786709906
OL,3,CUK economy races ahead of G7 pack in
OL,4,Cfirst half of 2026 despite Gulf war
OL,6,FIn truth, in the very short run,
OL,7,Fgovernments can do relatively little
OL,8,Fto influence the economy. Over the
OL,9,Flonger term, policy decisions can be
OL,10,Fenormously consequential.
OL,12,FMany economists argue that the
OL,13,Frelative "boom" of the Tony Blair
OL,14,Fyears was made possible, at least in
OL,15,Fpart, by reforms Margaret Thatcher
OL,16,Fenacted more than a decade earlier.
OL,18,FBurnham sounds like a man who wants to
OL,19,Freverse the 1980s. But maybe there
OL,20,Fwill be a difference between what he
OL,21,Fsays and what he does.
OL,26,@uD@JOUuD@OO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
